--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modifications made in Avalon
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Branched from FlClash v0.8.96 in 2026. The significant changes are:

  * A standalone node library. Single nodes (VLESS, VMess, Shadowsocks, Trojan,
    Hysteria2, TUIC, AnyTLS, SOCKS4/4a/5, HTTP(S), and Raw YAML/JSON records that
    cover every mihomo proxy type) can be created, edited and used without a
    subscription.

  * Multi-hop proxy chains. Nodes, proxy groups and existing local SOCKS/HTTP/HTTPS
    endpoints can be arranged as client -> prepend -> main -> append -> target and
    are compiled through `dialer-proxy` inside a single core instance.

  * Chain-to-profile binding, entry-group selection, compile diagnostics and path
    preview; export of nodes and chains as Clash config or JSON.

  * Embedded Tailscale session management, device inspection, Tailnet/subnet
    routing and exit-node preferences, with shared desktop and Android core APIs.

  * Desktop system-proxy integration, activity-aware UI telemetry and native
    window/IPC lifecycle improvements.

  * Renaming of the project and its identifiers: application name (FlClash ->
    Avalon), Dart package (fl_clash -> avalon), application identifiers
    (com.follow.clash -> com.masteralanlab.avalon), core and helper executables
    (FlClashCore / FlClashHelperService -> AvalonCore / AvalonHelperService), and
    the custom URL scheme (flclash:// -> avalon://).

Per-release summaries of changes are published with each GitHub Release.

